echo "text" - Linux will repeat text
whoami - says what accoutn you're using
id - gives you user information e.g
  uid --> Your User ID (a unique numerical identifier).
  gid -->  Your primary Group ID.
  groups --> All the groups you are a member of.
id -un - prints your username
pwd  - stands for "print working directory". It displays your current location in the file system. 
~ for your home directory
  home directory --> The home directory is a directory associated with a user name in the system's user account database
  current directory --> 
ls - shows contents in your current directory 
ls ~ - shows contents in your home directory
cd .. moves you to the directory above
cd ~
